# 📘 SSC CGL – Idioms & Phrases (PYQ) MCQ Practice Set – 1

---

### Q1.

He is **burning the midnight oil** to complete the project.
(a) Wasting time
(b) Working late at night
(c) Enjoying life
(d) Sleeping peacefully

---

### Q2.

She makes **a mountain out of a molehill**.
(a) Makes things difficult
(b) Exaggerates small things
(c) Becomes lazy
(d) Creates happiness

---

### Q3.

The soldiers were caught **red-handed**.
(a) With dirty hands
(b) While escaping
(c) In the act of committing crime
(d) After many years

---

### Q4.

This is a **Herculean task**.
(a) Very small task
(b) Very difficult task
(c) Very boring task
(d) Very dangerous task

---

### Q5.

He has to work hard to **make both ends meet**.
(a) Balance expenses
(b) Finish the work
(c) Become rich
(d) Achieve goals

---

### Q6.

Do not **cry over spilt milk**.
(a) Don’t be careless
(b) Don’t regret uselessly
(c) Don’t eat much
(d) Don’t lose hope

---

### Q7.

She is **spick and span** today.
(a) Very dirty
(b) Very active
(c) Very neat and clean
(d) Very rich

---

### Q8.

The news came **like a bolt from the blue**.
(a) Expected news
(b) Sudden shock
(c) Happy surprise
(d) Normal information

---

### Q9.

He always tries to **add fuel to the fire**.
(a) Solve problems
(b) Increase anger
(c) Put out fire
(d) Make peace

---

### Q10.

He passed the exam **with flying colours**.
(a) With great difficulty
(b) With great success
(c) Without preparation
(d) With average marks

---

---

# ✅ Answer Key

1 → (b) Working late at night
2 → (b) Exaggerates small things
3 → (c) In the act of committing crime
4 → (b) Very difficult task
5 → (a) Balance expenses
6 → (b) Don’t regret uselessly
7 → (c) Very neat and clean
8 → (b) Sudden shock
9 → (b) Increase anger
10 → (b) With great success

---

